    "text": "A copper complex crystallising in a CCP lattice with a cell edge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4518</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> has been revealed by employing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math>-ray diffraction studies. The density of a copper complex is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>62</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The molar mass of copper complex is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"bottom\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></menclose></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>gmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />(Nearest integer):&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo></math> Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>022</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></math>"
  },
